{
  "question": "What share of a business must service-disabled veterans own and control for SBA SDVOSB certification?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "For SBA SDVOSB certification, one or more service-disabled veterans must unconditionally and directly own at least 51 percent of the concern. The same service-disabled veterans must also control both the long-term decision-making and day-to-day operations of the business. This is a federal rule under 13 CFR part 128.",
